IC_kwDON91aY88AAAABCRCL6w","user":{"login":"ronny1020","id":46809311,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2ODA5MzEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46809311?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020","html_url":"https://github.com/ronny1020","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ronny1020/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T02:54:03Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T02:54:03Z","body":"With symlinks as a workaround, it's not required to link per file. Linking the whole folder works properly on my side. It's also consistent when adding a new skill.\n\n```bash\nln -s ../.claude/skills .agents/skills\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/4447046635/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":2,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/4459281623","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/31005#issuecomment-4459281623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/31005","id":4459281623,"node_id":"IC_kwDON91aY88AAAABCcs81w","user":{"login":"saero-robertpaul","id":217350546,"node_id":"U_kgDODPSBkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/217350546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul","html_url":"https://github.com/saero-robertpaul","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/saero-robertpaul/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-15T11:16:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-15T11:16:10Z","body":"Strongly agree this is the right ask, and the fact that Anthropic authored both MCP and the Skills spec makes the gap even more frustrating. While we wait for native AGENTS.md and .agents/skills/, the workaround I settled on is to keep one source-of-truth and compile it down to both .claude/ (skills + CLAUDE.md) and the AGENTS.md / .agents/skills/ layouts the other tools expect — I use xcaffold (https://github.com/saero-ai/xcaffold) for that. It’s not a substitute for first-class support, but it stops the dual-maintenance bleeding so we can stay on Claude Code without locking the rest of the team out. Happy to see this issue stay open until proper support lands.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/4459281623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/r